3. ⛔ CRITICAL — Swift 6.3.2 IRGen COMPILER CRASH (the root blocker).
   Every prior iOS/macOS build in this slot died with:
     swift-frontend … report_at_maximum_capacity(unsigned long)
       SmallVectorBase<unsigned int>::grow_pod → SyncCallEmission::setArgs
       IRGenSILFunction::visitFullApplySite
     4. While evaluating IRGenRequest for AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift
     5. While emitting IR SIL function "@$sSbScA_pSgIeAghyg_SbIeAghn_TR"
        = reabstraction thunk helper from
          @escaping @isolated(any) @callee_guaranteed @Sendable (Bool, Actor?) -> ()
          to @escaping @isolated(any) @callee_guaranteed @Sendable (Bool) -> ()
   Root cause: `Toggle("", isOn: Binding(get:{isOn}, set: onChange))` where
   `onChange: @MainActor (Bool) -> Void`. `Binding<Bool>` is `Sendable`, so the
   `@MainActor` setter is erased to an `@isolated(any) @Sendable` closure; the
   reabstraction thunk for that closure shape overflows an LLVM SmallVector in
   IRGen and aborts the compiler. It is DETERMINISTIC (the file never cached, so
   every retry re-hit it ~mid-build); it is NOT memory pressure (the symbol is
   the capacity-overflow path, not bad_alloc), and it post-dates the 88496 green
   run (AppearanceSettings was merged after). Fix (surgical, behaviour-identical):
     set: { newValue in MainActor.assumeIsolated { onChange(newValue) } }
   The Binding setter is now a plain non-isolated closure (SwiftUI always calls
   a setter on the main actor, so the assume holds), so no @isolated(any) thunk
   is emitted. PROOF the fix clears it: `xcodebuild build` →
   ** BUILD SUCCEEDED ** (the AppearanceSettings/ApiPlayground batch compiled),
   and the macOS leg now also reaches ** BUILD SUCCESSFUL ** (it shares the file).

4. TEST-BUNDLE ERRORS (surfaced for the first time once item 3 let the bundle
